00:00:14.001 --> 00:00:15.470
- Welcome to your Weekend Ticket.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.400
First we'll check out who came out on top

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.550
in last weekend's box office numbers.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:20.580
Then, we'll let you know what's new

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.070
in theaters this weekend.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:24.550
And, finally we'll leave
you with some new releases

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.116
to stream on FandangoNOW.

00:00:27.116 --> 00:00:29.017
(upbeat music)

00:00:29.017 --> 00:00:31.320
"Sonic the Hedgehog"
doesn't just gotta go fast,

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.140
it's gotta break records.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.160
The family friendly film had
the largest debut weekend ever

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.441
for video game adaptation,

00:00:37.441 --> 00:00:40.845
coming in with $58 million
over the traditional weekend,

00:00:40.845 --> 00:00:44.907
to last year's best of $54
million from "Detective Pikachu."

00:00:44.907 --> 00:00:46.690
"Sonic the Hedgehog" totaled $70 million

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.010
over President's Day, four-day weekend,

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.880
making it the fourth highest
President's Day weekend

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.420
of all time.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.180
That's a lot of rings.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.150
Speaking of breaking records,

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.060
last weekend's other new wide
release "Fantasy Island,"

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.160
a PG-13 update of the classic TV show

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.700
with an added Blumhouse
horror horror twist

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.120
became the highest
grossing horror film debut

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.700
of this year so far,

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.470
at $14 million after President's Day.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:15.530
And from presidents to the
current king of social media,

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:17.980
Bong Joon Ho's "Parasite" walked away

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.470
with four Oscars the previous weekend,

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.260
including becoming the
first-ever foreign language film

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.707
to win best picture.

00:01:24.707 --> 00:01:26.981
"Parasite" also returned
to 2,000 theaters,

00:01:26.981 --> 00:01:30.260
added $6.8 million to
its total box office,

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:34.330
and had a 234% increase in ticket sales.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.840
This marks the largest post-Oscars boost

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.710
for a best picture winner
in the past decade.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.840
The South Korean film entered the top ten

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:42.673
for the weekend,

00:01:42.673 --> 00:01:45.720
and became the fourth highest
grossing foreign language film

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.520
of all time in the U.S. at $45 million

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:53.520
and pushed its total gross
over $205 million worldwide.

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:55.508
(upbeat music)

00:01:55.508 --> 00:01:59.430
- [Doll] To live again he needed a friend.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.760
- The first new movie
heading theaters this weekend

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:05.430
is a horror movie sequel
called "Brahms: the Boy two."

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.800
This time around it's a
new story and a new cast,

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.550
but the same same director
and the same old creepy,

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:11.850
well-dressed doll.

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.700
When a family with a troubled
son moves into the guesthouse

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.870
of Hillshire mansion from the first movie,

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.340
it isn't long before they find Brahms.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.420
The son quickly becomes
eerily bonded to the doll

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.045
who seems to have upped
his creepy abilities.

00:02:25.045 --> 00:02:26.903
Sorry, Katie Holmes.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:30.020
Like I said, director
William Brent Bell returns

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:33.390
as does the writer of the
first movie Stacey Menear.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:34.780
So, if you liked the first movie,

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.730
you'll probably want to catch this one.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.260
(barks)

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.537
- I'm glad you're enjoying yourself.

00:02:41.537 --> 00:02:42.370
(water rushing)

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.850
- "The Call of the Wild"
also comes out this weekend.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.060
In this film adaptation
of the popular novel,

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.420
Harrison Ford teams up with
a hairy co-pilot once again,

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.190
this time it's a tortured
sled dog named Buck.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.697
After Buck is ripped from his home,

00:02:54.697 --> 00:02:57.730
sold as a sled dog, and
endures mistreatment,

00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:59.510
he eventually meets John Thornton,

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.370
and the two set off on
adventures in the wild,

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:04.000
testing their strength and bond.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.960
The novel is told from
Buck's point of view

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.670
and it looks like the film is staying true

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.030
to giving him a lot of personality.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:12.700
The CG Buck is a scan of
a real life dog adopted

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:15.310
by the director and his
motion capture is acted

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:19.020
by human, Terry Notary,
who also did the mo-cap

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.480
for Kong in Kong: Scull Island.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.770
Also, director Chris
Sanders has writing credits

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.510
on several movies you're
probably familiar with.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.837
Like "Aladdin," "Mulan,"
"Lilo and Stitch,"

00:03:29.837 --> 00:03:31.614
"How to Train Your Dragon,"
and "Beauty and the Beast,"

00:03:31.614 --> 00:03:33.756
just to name a few.

00:03:33.756 --> 00:03:35.350
(upbeat music)

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:38.170
There's also some great
movies that are now available

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.690
to stream at home on FandangoNOW.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.630
Let's start with Oscar
winner Jojo Rabbit.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.220
Taika Waititi won his first Oscar

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.500
for best adapted screenplay with this film

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.140
about a young kid growing up

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.397
in Germany during World War two.

00:03:52.397 --> 00:03:55.670
"Jojo Rabbit" is a satire that
follows a lonely, German boy

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.900
named Jojo, played by Roman Griffin Davis,

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.450
who idolizes Hitler and Nazis.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.810
But, he finds that his
loyalties are tested

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:05.140
when he learns his mother
is hiding a Jewish girl

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.460
in his house.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:08.280
The film stars Scarlett Johansson,

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.810
newcomer Roman Griffin
Davis, Sam Rockwell,

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:13.900
and writer, director
Taika Waititi as Hitler.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.960
As of this filming, the movie sits

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:19.510
at an 80% certified fresh
and an audience review score

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:23.460
of 95%, 'cause who doesn't
love Taika Waititi?

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:24.700
No one.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.620
No one doesn't like Taika Waititi.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.010
Now available to stream,

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:31.090
the Oscar nominated "Beautiful
Day in the Neighborhood."

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:32.900
While not a biopic on the life

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.660
of the lovable Fred
Rogers, this movie is based

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:37.150
on a real life story.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:37.983
The films tells the story

00:04:37.983 --> 00:04:40.733
about the reporter whose life
is touched by Mr. Rogers,

00:04:40.733 --> 00:04:43.810
as he learns more about the
man and his positive impact

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:45.420
on the world around him.

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:47.480
Tom Hanks of course plays Fred Rogers

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:50.090
and was given blessing and
praise from Mr. Rogers widow,

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.470
Joanne Rogers for his portrayal.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:55.290
And, if afterwards you want
a deeper biographical look

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.670
into Mr. Fred Rogers heartwarming life,

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:59.940
I recommend "Won't You Be My Neighbor."

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:03.450
Also available for digital
purchase on FandangoNOW.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.460
There's so much Mr. Rogers.

